CHANGES:
- New GET /api/auth/me BFF (Backend-for-Frontend) route for checking auth session
- Bridges frontend AuthProvider with backend /api/user/me endpoint

DETAILS:
- Reads httpOnly rumi_token cookie from the incoming Next.js request
- If no token found: immediately returns { authenticated: false, user: null }
- If token found: forwards to backend GET /api/user/me with Authorization: Bearer header
- Transforms backend user response into typed AuthMeResponse for frontend consumption
- If backend returns error (expired/invalid token): returns unauthenticated status
- Prevents Next.js from caching user data with cache: 'no-store' option
- This route is called by AuthProvider on every page load/refresh to restore session state
- Enables seamless session persistence across page navigations without exposing JWT to JS

